 3. Core Mechanics \u0026 Physics\n- **Metabolism:** Every block has a `Maintenance_Cost` (Electricity/Charge). Total Charge is shared across the body via a conductive graph. Resistance increases with distance from In-G/In-M nodes.\n- **Dynamic Growth/Decay:** If `Charge \u003e Threshold`, the body materializes a new block (randomly mutated). If `Charge \u003c 0`, the body loses blocks one by one.\n- **Minimum Life:** A cluster of `\u003c 5 blocks` ceases metabolism and becomes \"Junk.\"\n- **3D Physics:** Bodies use flexible joints (Ball-and-socket, Levers). Calculate `Torque` and `Stress`. If external force (currents or hunting) exceeds `Connection_Strength`, the body snaps and divides into two independent organisms.\n- **Behaviors:** \n    - **Hunting:** Physically tearing blocks from rivals to consume their Materia.\n    - **Parasitism:** Secretly docking to a host to drain their Charge.\n    - **Symbiosis:** Voluntary docking to share specialized functions (e.g., one filters G++, the other provides armor).\n\n### 4. Technical Implementation Requirements\n- **Configurability:** All constants (gas reactivity, mutation rates, energy costs) must be externalized in a `config.json` style format.\n- **Visual Style:** High-contrast retro-futurism. Polished brass, weathered copper, glowing vacuum tubes, and electrical arcs.\n- **Evolutionary Goal (Harmony):** Define Harmony as a state where `Metabolic_Stability` (n\u003dm growth/decay) is maintained despite a 70% change in environmental parameters.\n\n### 5. Your Immediate Task\n1. Generate the **Mathematical Engine** (Python or Pseudocode) for a single cycle of life, accounting for 3D lever stress and energy entropy across a 15-block body.\n2. Draft a **Mutation Table** (d100) that includes both beneficial (efficiency) and detrimental (explosive instability) outcomes.\n3. Describe the **Action-Survival** gameplay loop where a player-controlled organism must navigate an \"Acid Smoke Cloud\" (G--) to reach a \"Salt Depos