        "text": "). A high-contrast, tactile world of polished brass, weathered copper, glowing vacuum tubes, and oily reflections.\n\n### II. THE"
      }, {
        "text": " STORYBOOK (LORE \u0026 NARRATIVE)\n*   **Setting:** A planetary-scale junkyard."
      }, {
        "text": " Abandoned by \"The Inventors,\" it is a world of oil oceans and gas-choked skies.\n*   **Genesis"
      }, {
        "text": ":** UV radiation from the dying star hit an \"electric broth\" of discarded parts, sparking decentralized life.\n*   **The"
      }, {
        "text": " Philosophy:** There is no \"center\" or \"brain.\" Life is a collective property of the parts. If a body breaks, both"
      }, {
        "text": " halves—if large enough—continue to live.\n\n### III. DESIGN CONCLUSIONS (VISUALS \u0026 UI)\n*   "
      }, {
        "text": "**Geometry:** Truncated Octahedron modules. This allows for dense 3D packing and complex, flexible \"lever-"
      }, {
        "text": "and-joint\" branching.\n*   **The 7 Proto-Proteins (Blocks):**\n    1."
      }, {
        "text": "  **In-G (Gas Filter):** Turbine-like, draws in gases.\n    2.  **In"
      }, {
        "text": "-M (Scrap Magnet):** Mechanical claw, pulls in mineral salts (Materia).\n    3.  **In-I ("
      }, {
        "text": "Antenna/Eye):** Detects resource gradients and signals.\n    4.  **Out-G (Exhaust):** Rocket"
      }, {
        "text": " nozzle, provides reactive thrust.\n    5.  **Out-M (Waste Chute):** Secretes armor"
      }, {
        "text": " plates or \"Materia\" briquettes.\n    6.  **Out-I (Signal Lamp):** Communic"
      }, {
        "text": "ates vectors and blueprints to others.\n    7.  **Base Block (Chassis):** Structural skeleton, low power"
      }, {
        "text": " draw.\n*   **UI:** Analog gauges, trembling needles, and brass dials showing \"Charge\" and \"Pressure.\"\n\n###"
      }, {
        "text": " IV. GAMEPLAY \u0026 PHYSICS REGISTRY\n*   **Resource #1 (Charge):** Electricity flows through the body graph"
      }, {
        "text": ". Resistance increases with distance from input nodes. \n*   **Maintenance:** `Energy_Loss \u003d sum(Block"
      }, {
        "text": "_Base_Costs) * Stress_Multiplier (Lever Length)`. \n*   **Harmony Equation:** The body aims"
      }, {
        "text": " for $n\u003dm$ (Rate of new block synthesis \u003d Rate of old block decay). \n*   **"
      }, {
        "text": "Survival Rules:** \n    - Body \u003c 5 blocks \u003d Death (becomes Junk). \n    - Loss of"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003e 50% blocks \u003d Collapse unless Charge is sufficient to reboot.\n*   **Environment:** 5 Gas"
      }, {
        "text": " types (G-- to G++). G-- is highly reactive/unstable (high energy/high damage); G++ is lazy/"
      }, {
        "text": "inert (low energy/safe).\n*   **Interactions:** \n    - **Hunting:** Physical collision to break connections"
      }, {
        "text": ". \n    - **Parasitism:** Docking to drain a host\u0027s Charge.\n    - **Symb"
      }, {
        "text": "iosis:** Voluntary sharing of specialized block functions.\n\n### V. CONFIGURATION (CONFIGURABLE EVERYTHING)\nThe system"
      }, {
        "text": " must be driven by an external config (JSON/YAML) where all coefficients are modifiable:\n- `Mutation_Chance`:"
      }, {
        "text": " (Current: 0.05)\n- `Base_Maintenance`: (Current: 1.0)\n- "
      }, {
        "text": "`G_Reactivity_Scale`: (G--: 10.0 to G++: 0.1"
      }, {
        "text": ")\n- `Min_Body_Size`: (5)\n\n### VI. CURRENT DEVELOPMENT TASK\n**RESTORE ALL"
      }, {
        "text": " SYSTEMS AND PROCEED TO CODING:**\n1.  Initialize a 3D Physics environment (using a library like "
      }, {
        "text": "`PyBullet`, `Godot`, or a custom Matrix-based engine).\n2.  Implement the **Conductive"
      }, {
        "text": " Graph** logic: Calculate the Charge distribution across a 20-block body with one `In-G` at"
      }, {
        "text": " the tail and one `Out-G` at the head.\n3.  Calculate the **Lever Stress**: If the body"
      }, {
        "text": " is a 10-block long \"arm,\" determine the `Charge` cost to move the tip against a 3"
      }, {
        "text": "D oil current.\n4.  Generate a **Mutation Event**: Simulate the growth of a new block that has a 1"
      }, {
        "text": "0% chance to be a \"Turbo-Exhaust\" (High thrust, but leaks Charge).\n\n**Instruction to"
      }, {
        "text": " Agent:** Use the above data to build the core engine. All parameters must remain configurable. Begin by outputting the Architecture"
